note Converted from the Lapis prototype, attic/lapis/commands.lp.
note
note Lapis listed its commands in a table and hid their behaviour inside its
note PowerShell engine:
note   command show title (text) (renders a stylized title banner)
note In Shark a new instruction is declared with `to`, and the declaration is
note also the behaviour. Before anything is parsed, every new instruction is
note checked against conditions R1 to R6, so none of these can make the
note language ambiguous. See spec/03-clause-registry.md section 3.4.
note
note Two Lapis commands are not declared here:
note   `to page` is built into Shark, as `open page` and as the `to page` ending
note   of `show button`, so there is nothing to declare.
note   `show chart` and `show progress` were declared twice in Lapis, here and
note   in charts.lp. Shark forbids declaring an instruction twice (condition R5),
note   so they live once, in charts.shark.

note `share` lets a program that says `use commands` call it. See
note examples/lapis/showcase.shark.

share show title

note doc Renders a stylized title banner.
to show title the words as text
  centred
    show divider
    show text value of words
    show divider
